        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: விமானி",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "விமானி — vimāṉi — \"a pilot\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "விமானி பயணிகளுக்கு வணக்கம் சொன்னார். vimāṉi payaṇikaḷukku vaṇakkam coṉṉār. The pilot greeted the passengers."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "விமானம், a plane, + -இ, one who: the one who flies it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "விமானி (vimāṉi) is built from விமானம், \"an aeroplane\", borrowed from Sanskrit vimāna, \"a car of the gods\" (CDIAL 11823), with the ending -i, \"one who\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
